# Golden vectors for the MQTT 3.1.1 worked example.
#
# Written by paho-mqtt rather than by hand or by situ: each of these is what
# `paho.mqtt.client.Client` put on the socket, captured by standing a
# recorder in for the socket so that paho's own packet writer is the thing
# that ran. A description agreeing only with its own compiler has shown
# nothing, and these agree with the client the brokers are tested against.
#
#   c = Client(CallbackAPIVersion.VERSION1, client_id="situ",
#              clean_session=True)
#   c._sock = recorder
#   c._send_connect(60)
#   c._send_publish(0, b"a/b", b"hi", 0, False, False, MQTTMessageInfo(0))
#   ...
#
# They cover five of the fourteen arms of `packet`'s variant, chosen for the
# shapes rather than for the count: a CONNECT carrying the protocol name and
# an mqtt_string client id, a QoS-0 PUBLISH whose body has no packet
# identifier and a QoS-1 one whose body does, a SUBSCRIBE with its topic
# filter and requested QoS, and the two two-byte packets whose arm is
# `nothing` -- which is the arm a zero-length body has to reach.

packet connect      10 10 00 04 4D 51 54 54 04 02 00 3C 00 04 73 69 74 75
packet publish_qos0 30 07 00 03 61 2F 62 68 69
packet publish_qos1 32 10 00 08 73 65 6E 73 6F 72 2F 74 00 07 32 31 2E 35
packet subscribe    82 08 00 01 00 03 61 2F 62 00
packet pingreq      C0 00
packet disconnect   E0 00
